---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Section from "../components/ui/Section.astro";
import Button from "../components/ui/Button.astro";
import { email, mailto } from "../data/site";

// Low-friction contact. Every general "Get in touch" on the site lands here
// first, so this page has two jobs: say how a first conversation goes, and
// offer ONE explicit email action. Email is the working contact path, so the
// address is also shown as a large, selectable link — a `mailto:` link fails
// silently on managed devices and webmail-only setups.
//
// There is still no form: this is a static build with no server runtime, and
// no mail-sending credentials or form endpoint exist in the project. Inventing
// one would ship something that quietly loses enquiries. Adding a real form is
// follow-up work with a named dependency, not something to fake here.
//
// No response-time or support-hours promise anywhere on this page: those
// belong in a proposal or service agreement where they can be stated
// accurately for a specific client.

// Suggestions for the first email — prompts, not fields. They exist so the
// blank compose window is less blank, and so the reply can be useful first
// time rather than a round of questions.
const helpful = [
  "Your business, and roughly what it does",
  "Approximate team size",
  "What's happening now",
  "What you'd like to be different",
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Contact — tell us what you need | TWNY"
  description="Tell us what's happening in your business and we'll tell you what we'd do about it. You don't need to know which service you need before getting in touch."
>
  {/* OPENING — two columns at desktop: the reassurance on the left, the one
      email action on the right as a quiet panel. Below lg the panel follows
      the text, so the action is never above the explanation. */}
  <section class="bg-sand">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 sm:px-8 py-16 sm:py-24">
      <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1.1fr_0.9fr] lg:items-start lg:gap-20">
        <div>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-mineral mb-5">
            Contact
          </p>
          <h1
            class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold text-ink max-w-2xl text-balance"
          >
            Tell us what you need.
          </h1>
          <p class="mt-5 text-lg text-steel leading-relaxed max-w-xl text-pretty">
            You don't need to have all the answers, or to know which service
            you need. Tell us what's happening in your business and we'll
            tell you plainly what we'd do about it — including if that's less
            than you expected.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-base text-steel leading-relaxed max-w-xl text-pretty">
            Working out whether it's an ongoing Managed Technology arrangement,
            a defined piece of Professional Services work, or simply some
            advice is part of the conversation, not something you need to
            decide first.
          </p>
        </div>

        {/* The one email action. A lifted panel with a hairline, not a form:
            label, the address, the button, and four prompts. */}
        <div class="contact-panel rounded-sm border border-line bg-paper p-7 sm:p-8 lg:mt-1">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-mineral">
            Email TWNY
          </p>
          <a
            href={mailto}
            aria-label={`Email ${email}`}
            class="mt-4 inline-block font-display text-2xl font-medium leading-tight text-ink transition-colors hover:text-mineral-strong sm:text-[1.75rem] break-all"
            >{email}</a
          >
          <div class="mt-6">
            <Button href={mailto} variant="ember">Send an email</Button>
          </div>

          <p class="mt-9 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-steel">
            Helpful to include
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2.5">
            {
              helpful.map((line) => (
                <li class="grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-3 text-[0.9688rem] leading-[1.6] text-steel">
                  <span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-[0.7em] h-px w-3 bg-mineral/70" />
                  <span>{line}</span>
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-steel/90 text-pretty">
            All optional — a couple of lines is enough to start.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Section
    surface="paper"
    eyebrow="What happens next"
    heading="How a first conversation goes."
  >
    <ol class="border-t border-line max-w-2xl">
      <li class="grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-4 py-5 border-b border-line">
        <span class="font-mono text-mineral">01</span>
        <span class="text-[1.0313rem] leading-[1.6] text-steel text-pretty">
          You tell us roughly where you're at — the size of the team, what's
          working, and what isn't.
        </span>
      </li>
      <li class="grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-4 py-5 border-b border-line">
        <span class="font-mono text-mineral">02</span>
        <span class="text-[1.0313rem] leading-[1.6] text-steel text-pretty">
          We recommend a starting point — ongoing Managed Technology, a defined
          project, or sometimes just advice — with the scope written down.
        </span>
      </li>
      <li class="grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-4 py-5 border-b border-line">
        <span class="font-mono text-mineral">03</span>
        <span class="text-[1.0313rem] leading-[1.6] text-steel text-pretty">
          If it's a fit, we get started. If it isn't, we'll tell you that too,
          and point you somewhere better.
        </span>
      </li>
    </ol>

    {/* One plain statement of who this is for and how TWNY works. Deliberately
        unadorned — no "leading", no "full service", no address. */}
    <p class="mt-12 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-ink text-pretty">
      TWNY works with small and mid-sized Australian businesses through
      ongoing Managed Technology and defined Professional Services.
    </p>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
